TOPIC 1 : PL/SQL BASICS (SQL vs PL/SQL)
======================================================================

Q1. What is SQL?

Interview Ready Answer

SQL (Structured Query Language) is a declarative language used to
communicate with a relational database. It is used to retrieve,
insert, update, delete and define database objects.

Key Points

• Declarative language.
• Used to perform database operations.
• Executes one SQL statement at a time.
• Supported by Oracle, MySQL, SQL Server, PostgreSQL, etc.

======================================================================

Q2. What is PL/SQL?

Interview Ready Answer

PL/SQL (Procedural Language/Structured Query Language) is Oracle's
procedural extension to SQL. It combines SQL with programming
features like variables, loops, conditions, exception handling,
procedures, functions, packages and triggers.

Key Points

• Oracle specific language.
• Supports procedural programming.
• Executes as a PL/SQL block.
• Used to implement business logic inside the database.

Formula

PL/SQL = SQL + Programming Features

======================================================================

Q3. Why was PL/SQL introduced when SQL already existed?

Interview Ready Answer

PL/SQL was introduced because SQL is designed only for data
manipulation and cannot implement business logic. SQL does not
support variables, loops, conditions, exception handling,
procedures or functions.

PL/SQL overcomes these limitations by adding procedural programming
features, allowing developers to write complete database programs.

Limitations of SQL

• No variables.
• No IF-ELSE.
• No loops.
• No exception handling.
• No procedures or functions.
• Cannot implement business logic.

======================================================================

Q4. How does PL/SQL work internally?

Interview Ready Answer

PL/SQL code is first executed by the PL/SQL Engine. Whenever an SQL
statement is encountered, it is sent to the SQL Engine for execution.
After execution, control returns to the PL/SQL Engine.

Flow

User

↓

PL/SQL Engine

↓

SQL Engine

↓

Oracle Database

↓

Result Returned

Important Point

The entire PL/SQL block executes inside the Oracle Database,
reducing communication between the application and database.

======================================================================

Q5. Why is PL/SQL faster than executing multiple SQL statements from
an application?

Interview Ready Answer

PL/SQL executes the complete business logic inside the Oracle
database. Instead of sending multiple SQL statements separately,
the application sends a single PL/SQL block.

Advantages

• Reduces network round trips.
• Improves execution speed.
• Better performance.
• Less communication overhead.

======================================================================

Q6. What are the advantages of PL/SQL?

Interview Ready Answer

PL/SQL provides procedural programming capabilities along with SQL,
making database applications faster, secure and reusable.

Advantages

• Supports business logic.
• Supports variables.
• Supports IF-ELSE.
• Supports loops.
• Supports exception handling.
• Better performance.
• Reduced network traffic.
• Reusable procedures and functions.
• Better security using stored procedures.
• Easy maintenance.

======================================================================

Q7. What are the disadvantages of PL/SQL?

Interview Ready Answer

Although PL/SQL is powerful, it has some limitations.

Disadvantages

• Oracle specific language.
• Not portable to other databases.
• Vendor lock-in.
• Learning curve is higher than SQL.

======================================================================

Q8. Difference between SQL and PL/SQL.

Interview Ready Answer

SQL

• Declarative language.
• Used for database operations.
• Executes one statement at a time.
• Does not support variables.
• Does not support loops.
• Does not support IF-ELSE.
• No exception handling.
• Supported by multiple databases.

PL/SQL

• Procedural language.
• Used for business logic.
• Executes an entire block.
• Supports variables.
• Supports loops.
• Supports IF-ELSE.
• Supports exception handling.
• Oracle specific.

======================================================================

Q9. Where is PL/SQL used in industry?

Interview Ready Answer

PL/SQL is mainly used in Oracle-based enterprise applications where
business logic needs to be executed inside the database.

Industry Examples

• Banking Systems.
• Payroll Systems.
• ERP Applications.
• Hospital Management Systems.
• Oracle E-Business Suite.

