• SQL is used for data manipulation.
• PL/SQL is used for business logic.
• PL/SQL supports variables, loops, IF-ELSE and exception handling.
• PL/SQL executes inside Oracle Database.
• PL/SQL reduces network round trips.
• PL/SQL supports procedures, functions, packages and triggers.
• SQL is database independent.
• PL/SQL is Oracle specific.

